  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Advancing GCED and ESD to equip learners with skills and values to live safe and healthy lives, foster sustainable development, and engage with the world as creative and responsible global citizens</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Summary Description
In addressing the complex web of challenges, the Caribbean stands at a pivotal crossroads, prompting a fundamental re-evaluation of traditional educational paradigms. The current situation demands a comprehensive realignment of priorities, aiming not only to mitigate existing vulnerabilities but also to cultivate resilience and adaptability among Caribbean citizens. Education for Sustainable Development (ESD) and Global Citizenship Education (GCED) emerge as crucial issues to be embedded and mainstreamed in curricula. In this context, this workplan aims to strengthen education systems in the Caribbean to equip learners with the knowledge, skills, and values requisite to live safe and healthy lives,  foster  sustainable development, and engage with the world as creative and responsible global citizens.</narrative>
  </description>
